# Build-context allowlist.
#
# Everything is excluded by default and re-admitted one line at a time. This is deliberate: the
# build context is the repo root (the Dockerfiles need src/), and the repo root is also where the
# CodiEsp corpus, captured runs, kubeconfigs and gcloud credentials end up during a session. A
# deny-list would eventually leak one of them into a pushed image; an allow-list cannot.
#
# Adding a `!` line here is the ONLY way to get a file into an image. Do not add data/ or
# results/ — the trainer reads the corpus from the gcsfuse mount or the node filesystem at run
# time, never from inside the image.
*

!src
!docker

# ...and inside the two admitted trees, keep local junk out. Later patterns win, so these
# override the `!` lines above.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.ipynb_checkpoints
**/.pytest_cache
**/.DS_Store
docker/images.env
